<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Q3 GDP rises 3.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch Q3 GDP rises 3.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch third quarter gross domestic product (GDP) rose a provisional 3.0 percent year-on-year, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH GDP</p>
<p>			Q3 96	Q2 96	   Q1 96	   Q4 95</p>
<p> year-on-year	3.0     3.1 (2.8)     1.4 (1.8)     1.7 (1.6)</p>
<p>vs previous qtr</p>
<p> (seas. adj.)	0.7     1.6 (1.3)     0.0 (0.9)     0.6 (0.3)</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures show real percent changes. Previously announced figures in brackets.  </p>
<p>DUTCH GDP IN DETAIL</p>
<p> (real pct change yr/yr)	 Q3 96    Q2 96    Q1 96    Q4 95</p>
<p> private consumption		n.a.	3.0	3.5	2.0</p>
<p> government consumption	   n.a.	0.5	0.6	0.7</p>
<p> business investment		n.a.	2.7     -1.6	3.2</p>
<p> government investment	    n.a.	6.9     -6.1	0.3</p>
<p> exports goods and services     n.a.	0.9	4.3	6.4</p>
<p> imports goods and services     n.a.	0.9	2.7	4.3</p>
<p>NOTE - The GDP figures for the third quarter are the first estimates published by the CBS. A second estimate will be published early next year.</p>
<p>Because of the provisional nature of the third quarter estimate, separate figures were not published for the individual components of GDP.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Kelly, Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
